# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

tmp
regexped
target
tools/perftest/out
tools/perftest/*.txt
tools/re2test/re2-exhaustive.txt
tools/re2test/re2-adjusted.txt
tools/re2test/re2test
tools/perftest/perftest
examples/**/*.wasm
# A component's sibling .wit is generated by `regexped compile`, like a stub.
# Named rather than globbed, so a hand-written .wit an example ships is not
# hidden with them.
examples/wasmtime/rust/secrets/secrets.wit
examples/wasmtime/rust/secret-scanner/component/secrets.wit
examples/wasmtime/rust/secret-scanner/component/.built
examples/wasmtime/rust/secrets/.component.stamp
# The C example's component build puts every artefact in its own directory.
examples/wasmtime/c/url-parts/component/
examples/wasmtime/c/url-parts/wasip2/
examples/**/stub*.*
examples/**/regexp.*s
Cargo.lock
wasm-merge
/wasm-tools
/wac
# `make docker` assembles the build context in docker/: the regexped binary is
# copied there and the three tools are fetched there. `regexped` and
# `wasm-merge` above are unanchored and already cover their copies; these two
# are anchored to the repo root, so their docker/ counterparts need naming.
/docker/wasm-tools
/docker/wac
examples/workers/.wrangler
node_modules
package-lock.json
plans/
tools/likelytest/likelytest
tools/setperf/setperf
tools/setperf/*.txt
tools/fuzz/found
tools/pattest/pattest
tools/settest/settest
tools/re2test/make_sets/make_sets
tools/likelytest/*.txt

# TypeScript build output of the Node examples
examples/node/*/dist/
